  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mokoro Ltd 2017-2018,WIDE bridging - Mokoro Ltd 2017-2018, WIDE Bridging</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Mokoro Ltd 2017-2018,WIDE forts&#xe4;ttning</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen syftar till fortsatt forskning inom WIDE-projektet  (Wellbeing and Illbeing Dynamics in Ethiopia), som handlar om att f&#xf6;rst&#xe5; hur det etiopiska samh&#xe4;llet har f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndrats och utvecklats under snabb, nationell ekonomisk tillv&#xe4;xt samt under p&#xe5;verkan fr&#xe5;m m&#xe5;nga utvecklingsisattser fr&#xe5;n internationella givare och andra organisationer. I tre omg&#xe5;ngar har kvalitativa studier genomf&#xf6;rts p&#xe5; 20 platser/omr&#xe5;den runt om i Etiopien.
Mer specifikt har den h&#xe4;r insatsen tv&#xe5; komponenter: 
1) Fortsatt, f&#xf6;rdjupad forskning inom fyra av de tidigare WIDE omr&#xe5;dena med fokus p&#xe5;: a) politiska och ekonomiska trender, s&#xe4;rskilt syssels&#xe4;ttning och politisk styrning. b) Hur har omr&#xe5;dena reagerat p&#xe5; f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar inom landanv&#xe4;ndning och urbanisering, p&#xe5;verkan fr&#xe5;n torka och hur ser ungas ekonomiska situation ut. c) Hur har oj&#xe4;mliket utvecklats i omr&#xe5;dena.  
2) Att f&#xf6;rbereda f&#xf6;r den fj&#xe4;rde fasen (WIDE-4), som mer ska integreras med Etiopiska institutioner och hur man b&#xe4;st ska kunna n&#xe5; ut med resultaten fr&#xe5;n forskningen till Etiopiska universitet och makthavare.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This contribution is a continuation of the previously supported WIDE-Project (Wellbeing and Illbeing Dynamics in Ethiopia), which have been going on during the past 20 years in three phases. The research is qualitative and focuses on 20 rural areas in Ethiopia and how they have transformed during a period of rapid, national economic growth and development efforts. 
More specifically this contribution has two Components:
1)  Continued research in three, of the previous 20 areas, with focus on: a) political and economical transformation, especially livelihoods and political governance. b) Experience of these areas in three important policy areas; land use and local urbanisation, impact and reaction to droughts and the economic experience of young people in the communities. c) How have inequality developed and transformed in the communities.  
2) To prepare for the fourth phase (WIDE-4), that aim to institutionalize the WIDE program with Ethiopian agencies and how to beast reach out with results to Ethiopian Universities, policy makers and decision makers.</narrative>
  </description>
